{"title":"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Fermat buys <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> bananas and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> apples. The cost of each banana is half the cost of each apple. If the total cost of the fruit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f8f539c1b3a2c8df6aa0be01f15ec1342734b1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$16.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />, what is the cost of each apple?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0947a55615f31f22338ff30cab1d8bfeb4425c59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\$0.50 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\$1.33 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\$4.00 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\$2.67 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\$2.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"550\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Banana_as_Variable.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Banana_as_Variable)\">Solution 1 (Banana as Variable)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Banana as Variable)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be the cost of each banana. Since each banana costs half as much as each apple, each apple must cost <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9b30259d95f64f9aa7c6bd36e1583618a23c8bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />. Since Fermat bought <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> bananas and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> apples and the total price was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f8f539c1b3a2c8df6aa0be01f15ec1342734b1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$16.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />, we then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/d/edd8fd45b85c2b05bac92b6666efbba1bdc6aadb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8b + 4(2b) = \\$16.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/6692b47acab91aadfa3945e0cf9ca61509e647e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8b + 8b = \\$16.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"133\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/7/1b75519f2518064ebb6f4f99545d08113e9511bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16b = \\$16.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>We can then see that the cost of each banana is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c78cd0de09afc053c5a7244659a936a9c59df2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />. The cost of each apple is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/c/6ac04896abeb449cd9c426731c7f0f3bbb073242.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1.00 \\times 2 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } \\$2.00}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"185\" height=\"31\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Apple_as_Variable.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Apple_as_Variable)\">Solution 2 (Apple as Variable)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Apple as Variable)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the cost of each apple. Since each banana costs half as much as each apple, each banana must cost <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/f/9afddc3c61aa4e66d003d0c7cc5bd01560d341f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" />. Since Fermat bought <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> bananas and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> apples and the total price was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f8f539c1b3a2c8df6aa0be01f15ec1342734b1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$16.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />, we then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/9/ab9444985a4986403b61f31455f975f55b0f572e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8(\\frac{a}{2}) + 4a = \\$16.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec2d2ec4dcf456a92e39c18892bc964a436e48c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4a + 4a = \\$16.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69f717c563169ead9e1811dcbdaa814387afad36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8a = \\$16.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a0504dec37fcc242ee2bdd3fcf670ae5dee0b402.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{\\$16.00}{8} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } \\$2.00}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"201\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat\">2026 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\